{
  "_comment": "Shared by client/core/test/providers.test.ts and server/internal/provider/template_test.go, so the two implementations of the template grammar cannot drift. Inputs are already-parsed URL parts (pathname, search), not whole URLs: URL parsing differs between a browser and Go at the edges, the grammar must not. The one exception is \"pathnames\": the Go port resolves dot segments itself (net/url does not), so it must give what URL.pathname gives. \"urls\" are whole URLs: only a plain URL (a grammar both ports check the same way) may appear in an example or a watch template, and for a plain one this port's parse must give what URL gives. Outside it net/url and WHATWG disagree (tabs, backslashes, \"|\", ports over 65535, numeric hosts). No descriptor host or plain URL may have an \"xn--\" label: Node and net/url take \"xn--a\" or \"xn--\" as text, a browser runs UTS46 and refuses them.",
